{% comment %}
  InstaMom University — the shipping-window promise, shown under the buy buttons
  on a product page.

  Owner's launch copy, verbatim:
    "Orders will ship as soon as possible but no later than 7-10 business days.
     As supply chains shift some items may be replaced with similar items of
     equal value."
    "Pre-order now, all Welcome Boxes begin shipping on Friday August 14th, 2026"

  That pre-order line is retired. Owner, 13 Aug 2026 — the eve of that date —
  asked for "now shipping" instead, so the lead now says the wait is over rather
  than naming a date. Changed here as well as on the badge because the two render
  on the same product page: a "NOW SHIPPING" badge above a "Pre-order now, begins
  shipping Friday August 14" note is the store contradicting itself.

  (The earlier wording was "all Welcome Boxes"; Virginia's 3 Aug email put Warm
  Hug from Home and Room Refresh on the same date and neither is a Welcome box,
  so the line went product-neutral.)

  Both sentences are promises, so they have to agree with the Shipping &
  Delivery Policy (7–10 business days processing, and the substitution clause in
  its §8). If one changes, change the other — shopify/content/policy-shipping.html.

  The lead is driven by its own `ships-aug-14` tag, NOT by a combination of
  `pre-order` and `welcome-week`. That combination looked equivalent when only
  Welcome Week Starter was pre-order — but Homesick Helper also carries
  `welcome-week`, so the moment it opened for sale it would have silently started
  claiming a ship status it has no basis for. Shipping is a promise; it gets an
  explicit tag, and adding a box to it is a tag away.

  The tag NAME is historical now that the date is gone from the copy — read it as
  "in the 14 August wave", i.e. shipping. It was not renamed because that is a
  write to three live products, not a theme edit. Keep it in step with
  snippets/instamom-badge.liquid, which keys off the same tag.

  No date is hard-coded here any more, so nothing in this snippet goes stale on a
  calendar. A product that should NOT read as shipping loses the tag.

  Usage: {% render 'instamom-shipping-note', product: product %}
  Styling: .instamom-shipnote* in assets/instamom.css
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign ships_aug_14 = false
  if product.tags contains 'ships-aug-14'
    assign ships_aug_14 = true
  endif
-%}

<div class="instamom-shipnote">
  {%- if ships_aug_14 -%}
    <p class="instamom-shipnote__lead">
      <strong>Now shipping.</strong> No pre-order wait &mdash; orders go out on
      the schedule below.
    </p>
  {%- endif -%}
  <p class="instamom-shipnote__body">
    Orders ship as soon as possible, and no later than 7&ndash;10 business days.
    As supply chains shift, some items may be replaced with similar items of
    equal value.
  </p>
</div>
